      "comparability_note": "Not a like-for-like high-level comparison: the reference (ops-nn/norm/batch_norm_v3/op_kernel/arch35/batch_norm_v3_regbase_common.h) is a register-based SIMT micro-API (\"regbase\") kernel using MicroAPI::CreateMask/RegTensor/LoadDist/StoreDist, while pyasc2 deliberately emits only the AscendC high-level API (no micro-api). The register-resident reduction is a structural advantage pyasc2 cannot express, so this miss is SIMT-attributable (and additionally DMA-bound), not a pyasc codegen bug. Contrast add (add_dag.h), a high-level Vec DAG that pyasc2 matches at ratio 1.18. See docs/perf-vs-ascendc-demo.md \"Reference programming model\".",
